# A byte order mark is valid JSON inside a string, and is ignored at the
# start of a file. The file is generated with strconv-unquote so that
# the otherwise invisible character is explicit.
# This case is wrongly rejected; see https://cuelang.org/issue/3399.

strconv-unquote '"﻿{\"a\": \"x﻿y\"}"'
cp stdout x.json
! exec cue export x.json
stderr 'invalid JSON'
